@startuml bpu_lookahead
title IBPU internals: m-entry forecast, fast path and timed slow correction
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 95

legend left
  [E] Existing gem5 call or signal
  [N] New IBPU / bridge / helper connection
  [A] Model algorithm; illustrative private operation
  This is the custom uBTB/mBTB model, not a required IBPU topology.
endlegend

participant Gem5BpuBridge as Bridge
participant "CustomBPU : IBPU" as BPU
participant "AddressGenerator\nprivate model helper" as AG
participant "mBTB\nprivate evaluation context" as MBTB
participant "uBTB" as UBTB
participant "BpuHistory / PredictionLedger" as History
participant "ForecastCache\nprivate host optimization" as Forecast
participant "model pipeline / ResponseQueue" as Responses

Bridge -> BPU : [N] tick(now: Cycles, credits)
note over BPU, Responses
  Backend/predecode feedback has already been applied by the bridge.
  m = host batch size; n = slow-predictor pipeline latency.
  AddressGenerator/ForecastCache and [A] operations are private helpers,
  not new O3 stages or existing gem5 APIs.
end note

group First: progress modeled work already issued
    BPU -> Responses : [A] collect due completions(now), even if FTQ is full
    note over BPU
        bpu tahminlerini queue'dan çağırır.
    end note
    loop each due completion, in modeled event/age order
        Responses --> BPU : [A] (key, source, result, history lineage)
        alt request was invalidated by an older recovery
            BPU -> History : [A] release canceled request metadata once
        else fast result is due
            BPU -> Responses : [A] publish provisional BpuFetchTarget at ready_u
        else slow result is due for a still-live source prediction
            BPU -> History : [A] find the matching fast prediction by key
            BPU -> BPU : [A] compare CFI identity, direction, target,
            BPU -> BPU : [A] block boundaries and next-CFI/span
            alt fast and slow agree
                BPU -> History : [A] mark slow validation complete
            else a correction is required
                BPU -> Responses : [A] enqueue OverrideEvent at ready_m + redirectDelay
                note over Bridge, BPU
                  Bridge processes peekOverride() after tick() returns.
                  Local correction or asynchronous O3 arbitration is shown
                  in mbtb_late_recover.puml. Wrong-path queries may continue
                  until the effective override deadline; comparator-time
                  throttling would be a separate explicit model policy.
                end note
            end
        end
    end
    BPU -> Responses : [A] check control events with readyCycle <= now
    BPU -> BPU : [A] fence affected new issue for a due, still-live override
    note over BPU, Responses
      A due override fences new affected queries until bridge arbitration.
      Before that deadline, redirectDelay does not silently stop the path.
      Previously issued completions still progress under their own policy.
    end note
end

group Second: prepare host forecasts, without publishing future work
    BPU -> Forecast : [A] check cached candidates and dependency versions
    alt forecast empty, invalid, or unable to cover the current path
        BPU -> History : [A] obtain isolated forecast state at source checkpoint
        BPU -> AG : [A] generateBatch(queryPC, m, forecastState)
        loop up to m dependent predictions; stop at unknown feedback dependency
            AG -> MBTB : [N] lookup(BTBQuery{addr = nextQueryPC})
            MBTB --> AG : [N] BTBResult{cfi_list, commitData}
            AG -> AG : [A] run model direction/target selection for ordered CFIs
            AG -> AG : [A] stop block at first taken; form ordered blocks
            AG -> History : [A] advance forecast-only history/checkpoints
            AG -> AG : [A] derive nextQueryPC from this prediction
            AG -> Forecast : [A] cache candidate + dependency versions + metadata
        end
        AG --> BPU : [A] batch prepared; no simulated time has elapsed
    end
end

group Third: admit new modeled queries only within hardware resources
    alt issue interval, pipeline/output credits and recovery state allow work
        BPU -> History : [A] allocate dynamic key and source checkpoint
        BPU -> UBTB : [N] lookup(BTBQuery{addr = liveQueryPC})
        UBTB --> BPU : [N] fast prediction candidates
        BPU -> BPU : [A] record accepted issue_u; schedule fast result
        BPU -> Forecast : [A] find candidate matching PC, lineage and table/history version
        alt matching forecast is still valid at slow lookup sampling time
            Forecast --> BPU : [A] reusable slow candidate and metadata
        else mismatch, wrong path or intervening relevant training
            BPU -> MBTB : [N] lookup(query) in the correct modeled context
            MBTB --> BPU : [N] recomputed slow candidates
            BPU -> Forecast : [A] invalidate dependent cached suffix
        end
        BPU -> Responses : [A] record issue_m and schedule slow completion
        BPU -> History : [A] apply live speculative updates exactly once,
        BPU -> History : [A] according to the model's stage/history policy
    else no modeled capacity, not yet issue time, or affected recovery pending
        BPU -> BPU : [A] hold new issue; keep ready results and due control events
    end
end
BPU --> Bridge : [N] tick returns; bridge may now handle overrides and ready data

note over BPU, Responses
  Stall-free example: issue_u = issue_m = 0, latency_u = 1, n = 4.
  Fast result is visible at cycle 1; slow result is visible at cycle 4.
  With redirectDelay = 0, provisional-path work may occur in cycles 1..3.
  The source's slow deadline does not restart when host code detects a mismatch.
  Accepted slow issue, initiation interval and stage stalls determine ready_m.
end note
note over History, Forecast
  Forecast evaluation must isolate lookup side effects, RAS/history,
  replacement/random state and statistics from live simulated state.
  Replay updates only at modeled times; invalidate/recompute on dependencies.
  m must not grant extra hardware buffer slots or future training knowledge.
  If frozen-table batching intentionally changes results, label that as an
  approximate model; it is not equivalent to cycle-by-cycle execution.
end note
note over UBTB, Responses
  Each following accepted fast query uses the live fast-path cursor.
  On disagreement, it may follow the wrong path until a due override applies.
  Wrong-path queries need their own keys, history and resource accounting;
  never compare them by index against unrelated mBTB forecast entries.
end note
@enduml
